  "title": "P0128 — Coolant Thermostat Below Regulating Temperature",
  "source": "dtc-reference.md",
  "score": 0.2024,
  "content": "P0128 — Coolant Thermostat Below Regulating Temperature\nThe engine is not reaching its target operating temperature in the expected time,\nalmost always a thermostat stuck open. Impact is moderate: reduced fuel economy,\nhigher emissions, and a cabin heater that underperforms in cold weather.\nRecommended action: schedule thermostat replacement within the week; not an\nimmediate safety issue but worsens fuel cost across a fleet."
}
{
  "title": "C0561 — System Disabled Information Stored (ABS/ESC)",
  "source": "dtc-reference.md",
  "score": 0.1869,
  "content": "C0561 — System Disabled Information Stored (ABS/ESC)\nThe anti-lock braking / electronic stability control system has disabled itself\nand stored a fault. This is a high-severity chassis code: the driver may have\nreduced braking assistance. Recommended action: remove from service immediately\nand inspect wheel-speed sensors, ABS module power/ground, and related wiring\nbefore returning the vehicle to a route."
}
{
  "title": "P0420 — Catalyst System Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)",
  "source": "dtc-reference.md",
  "score": 0.1719,
  "content": "P0420 — Catalyst System Efficiency Below Threshold (Bank 1)\nThe catalytic converter on bank 1 is no longer converting exhaust gases\nefficiently. This is frequently a downstream symptom of a chronic misfire or a\nfailing oxygen sensor rather than the converter itself. Severity is medium: the\nvehicle is drivable but will fail emissions testing and fuel economy degrades.\nRecommended action: resolve any active misfire codes first, verify the rear O2\nsensor, then re-evaluate before replacing the converter (an expensive part)."
}

