{
  "title": "P0301 — Cylinder 1 Misfire Detected",
  "source": "dtc-reference.md",
  "score": 0.2748,
  "content": "P0301 — Cylinder 1 Misfire Detected\nA misfire on cylinder 1 means combustion is incomplete or absent. Common causes\nare worn spark plugs, failing ignition coils, clogged fuel injectors, or low\ncompression. Driving with an active misfire risks unburned fuel damaging the\ncatalytic converter and can leave a driver stranded. Recommended action: pull the\nvehicle from service and schedule inspection within 24 hours. Start by swapping\nthe coil and plug for cylinder 1, then re-test under load."
}

